        "Title": "A Guide for the Perplexed",
        "Description": "<p><strong>\"[An] intense, multilayered story.\" \u2014Jami Attenberg, <em>New York Times Book Review</em></strong></p><p>Software prodigy Josie Ashkenazi has invented an application that records everything its users do. When she visits the Library of Alexandria as a tech consultant, she is abducted in Egypt's postrevolutionary chaos with only a copy of the philosopher Maimonides' famous work to anchor her\u2014leaving her jealous sister Judith free to take over her life. A century earlier, Cambridge pr...",
