        "Title": "Small Gods",
        "Description": "<p><strong>\u201cPratchett\u2019s <em>Monty Python</em>-like plots are almost impossible to describe. His talent for characterization and dialogue and his pop-culture allusions steal the show.\u201d\u2014<em>Chicago Tribune</em></strong></p><p><strong>No sacred cow is left unskewered in this intriguing installment in Sir Terry Pratchett's internationally bestselling Discworld series, a divinely funny take on organized religion, petty gods, and the corrupting thirst for power.</strong></p><p>Religion is a compe...",
